A structured threat analysis using STRIDE categories was applied to the wearable and its communications.

Threat Vector Mitigation
Spoofing Injecting false sensor signals or faked alert messages TEE‑authenticated sensor data; alert packages digitally signed; rate‑limiting on alerts (max 3 Tier‑2/3 per hour per device before forced cool‑down)
Tampering Physical device tampering to disable alerts or extract keys Secure element, tamper‑evident enclosure, integrity check at boot; device locks if enclosure opened
Repudiation User denies generating an alert Hardware‑signed alert with cryptographic proof of origin; audit trail
Information disclosure Eavesdropping on wireless transmissions All links encrypted (DTLS 1.3, AES‑256‑GCM); no raw sensor data transmitted
Denial of service Jamming of radio frequencies Multi‑radio fallback; satellite band (L‑band) is narrowband and robust; local buffering with retry; mesh relay as additional path
