10. Terminology and Long‑Term Vision

We explicitly reject the “digital immune system” framing. Instead, Guardian AI is described as a personal safety mesh—a distributed, opt‑in network in which devices cooperate to bridge coverage gaps and speed verified alerts, while preserving individual autonomy and strict privacy. The long‑term vision is a world where emergency response is proactive but never surveillant, where technology compresses the time between distress and help without eroding civil liberties. This blueprint provides the technical, mathematical, and organisational foundation to realise that vision in a phased, ethically disciplined manner.


