Appendix B — Operator Capacity Model and Staffing Tables

We provide detailed staffing calculations for monitoring centre operations.

Input parameters:

· Subscribers N (in thousands).
· False Tier‑2 rate per user-year: f = 1.0 (before adaptive threshold; with adaptation, effective rate drops to 0.4 for active adults, but we conservatively use 1.0 for planning).
· True Tier‑2 incident rate per user-year: t = 0.05.
· Average handling time (AHT) for Tier‑2: 30 seconds (review + call attempt). Standard deviation 15 seconds.
· Operator working hours: 8 hours/day, 5 days/week, 365 days/year coverage requires shifts.
· Shrinkage factor (breaks, training, sick leave): 1.3.

Formula:
Total annual Tier‑2 alerts = N \cdot (f + t).
Daily alerts = annual / 365.
Total daily workload (seconds) = Daily alerts × 30.
Operators per shift = Total workload / (8 × 3600) × 1.3.
We round up to nearest integer.

