Appendix E — Phase 0 Dataset and Field Study Protocol

Objective: Build a labelled dataset of acoustic and kinematic signals during real or simulated physical assault/distress events to train and validate the Duress Score classifier.

Study design:

· Partner institutions: Level I trauma centres, domestic violence shelters, police training academies.
· Data collection:
  · Simulated: Actors perform scripted assault scenarios (push, grab, strike) under controlled safety conditions, wearing the device in multiple positions. Supervised by stunt coordinators and medical staff.
  · Real‑world: With consent, survivors of violent incidents can contribute anonymised sensor data from the device (if worn during the event) collected retrospectively via forensic download.
· Data labelling: Each event is labelled by type (assault, accidental fall, medical, no emergency) by a panel of medical and law enforcement experts using video corroboration.
· Target size: Minimum 10,000 positive assault/distress samples and 50,000 negative samples across diverse demographics.
· IRB oversight: Full ethical review; data stored with differential privacy; participants can withdraw.

The dataset will be used exclusively for internal algorithm development and will not be sold or shared. The duress classifier will only be deployed after achieving >95% sensitivity and >90% specificity on a held‑out test set, with fairness metrics across race, gender, and age.

